# verify-before-act-universal-gate

Every physical action in the warehouse (move, package, transport, container selection) must pass through a multi-layered pre-condition verification gate before the action is initiated. No single check is sufficient; the pattern recurs across lot identity, system confirmation, container state, and environmental conditions. Skipping any check invalidates the entire gate.

## Procedures
- Before initiating any physical move: confirm lot ID matches, confirm IMS pre-move update is confirmed, verify container availability and condition, check for flags or disqualifiers.
- Treat each verification as a hard gate — a pending or failed check is a hard stop, not a soft advisory.
- Perform checks in dependency order: system state (IMS) → lot identity → container qualification → environmental clearance (corridor hours, cleanroom class).

## Conventions
- No physical action proceeds until ALL applicable gates are cleared.
- A partial check set is treated the same as no check.

